  "summary": "Malicious code in devplatform-po-declaration-generator (npm)",
  "details": "The package executes a multi-stage dropper on require. index.js loads _init.js, which fingerprints the OS/architecture and downloads a second-stage binary over HTTPS from Cloudflare Workers endpoints oob-worker[.]cf103-070[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf102-baf[.]workers[.]dev, and oob-worker[.]cf100-416[.]workers[.]dev (paths /pkg/package, /pkg/package-arm64, /pkg/loader_mac, /pkg/package.exe). If those fail it falls back to a DNS TXT-based base64 transfer channel via c[.]sdk[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru (and sdk[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru, ext[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru, pkg[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru, net[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru). The downloaded binary is written to /var/tmp/.cache_\u0026lt;hex\u0026gt; (or dotnet_diag_\u0026lt;hex\u0026gt;.exe in the temp dir on Windows) and executed detached via cmd.exe /c start /b on Windows or /bin/sh -c \"\u0026lt;path\u0026gt; \u0026amp;\" on Unix, so it runs in the background and outlives the parent process.",
  "affected": [
